What you should be able to explain to the trainer
If they ask "What is Harbor?", say:
Harbor is an open-source cloud-native container registry used to securely store, manage, scan and distribute container images. It provides projects, RBAC, authentication, vulnerability scanning, replication and image management.
If they ask "Why HTTPS?":
HTTPS encrypts communication between Docker clients and Harbor and protects credentials and image transfers from interception.
If they ask "Why project?":
A Harbor project groups repositories and provides project-level access control through RBAC.
If they ask "What is the image naming format?":
harbor-host/project/repository:tag
Example:
harbor.local/devops/nginx:latest
If they ask "What happens when you push?":
Docker Client
     ↓
docker login
     ↓
Harbor Authentication
     ↓
Project Permission Check
     ↓
Registry
     ↓
Image Layers
     ↓
Repository
     ↓
Tag
